new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b897563
--- /dev/null
+++ b/crates/vp-tun/PROXY_DNS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,141 @@
+# Explicit mobile DNS policy (candidate)
+
+This implements the missing privacy boundary; socket protection alone is not a
+privacy guarantee. Product engine remains vp_core. No public provider is selected.
+
+## Product contract agreed for the next candidate
+
+- C ABI stays 1.1. Connect **payload** `schemaVersion: 2`; outer command envelope and NodeProfile
+  remain version 1. Host checks advertised `connectPayloadVersions` before consent.
+- Required `dns.bootstrapServers`: 1..4 numeric `SocketAddr` values.
+- Required `dns.user`: `{ "route": "selected_proxy", "servers": [...] }`, with
+  1..4 explicit numeric resolver endpoints selected/configured by the user.
+- Ports nonzero; unspecified/multicast addresses rejected; IPv4/IPv6 accepted.
+  User upstreams reject nonzero IPv6 scope/flow info because proxy address
+  encodings cannot preserve them.
+- Legacy ambiguous `dnsServers` is rejected with `UPGRADE_INCOMPATIBLE` before action,
+  not reinterpreted. No direct user-DNS option is implemented in this candidate.
+- Underlying OS DNS may seed **bootstrap only**, never silently user DNS.
+- A missing user resolver blocks connection and asks for settings; no hardcoded
+  public DNS and no fallback from a private/unreachable resolver to public/direct.
+- Current b739844 guest APK remains a historical **direct-protected UDP DNS**
+  fixture. It is not changed or retroactively claimed to certify this policy.
+
+## Core API / integration ownership
+
+`vp_dns::Resolver::bootstrap(Vec<SocketAddr>, &endpoint_host) -> Result<Resolver>`
+is pure construction. It binds bootstrap resolution to that exact proxy endpoint
+(name comparison folds ASCII and strips a terminal dot); CNAME following remains
+part of that endpoint lookup. Socket purpose is `Bootstrap` and upstream endpoints
+are numeric, eliminating resolver bootstrap recursion.
+
+`vp_core::host_network::HostNetwork::bootstrap_host() -> Option<String>` defaults
+to None. A protected `lookup_host` permits only this configured endpoint. Numeric
+addresses need no DNS. Distinct SOCKS UDP relay domain names and TUIC peer-returned
+domain names fail closed rather than leak direct DNS. Once bootstrap_host is set,
+`Purpose::Dns` direct sockets are rejected, and Bootstrap destinations must belong
+to the configured list, before the platform hook is invoked.
+
+`vp_tun::user_dns::UserDns::selected_proxy(Arc<dyn vp_core::Outbound>,
+Vec<SocketAddr>) -> vp_common::Result<UserDns>` is pure. The mobile adapter supplies
+the exact selected proxy (its typed node contract excludes Direct); it never uses
+a router that could select Direct. UDP support is mandatory before startup.
+
+`vp_tun::run_with_device_proxy_dns(cfg, tag, ctx, Arc<UserDns>, device)` intercepts
+both UDP destination port 53 and TCP destination port 53. TCP uses DNS's two-byte
+length prefix and sequential bounded frames; UDP retains each datagram. Both are
+sent through the selected proxy to the explicit numeric user resolver. Other
+ports use the normal selected outbound path. No fake-IP answers or assumptions.
+
+Mobile owner integrates adapter+ABI metadata+fixtures, Android owner integrates
+bootstrap and pre-consent version check, data owner integrates settings/typed
+payload and user-facing route/resolver disclosure. Pipeline owner promotes the
+patch only after checks and the frozen guest baseline window. This document does
+not claim that those consumers or an Android APK are already integrated.
+
+## Safety and semantics
+
+- 64 active intercepted DNS flows; excess flows dropped before spawning a task.
+- 64 simultaneous exchanges; no unbounded exchange queue. 256 requests per flow.
+- 4096-byte message cap for both transports, 5-second whole exchange/write budget,
+  10-second client-frame idle/read budget. Larger TCP messages are unsupported.
+- UDP answers are clamped to the client's EDNS size (512 without OPT) and the
+  actual IP/UDP MTU payload budget. Oversize answers become valid DNS TC replies,
+  never ipstack's truncated/split datagrams; TCP retry retains the proxy policy.
+- One fresh proxy session per query, round-robin only among explicitly configured
+  servers. No retry or cross-policy fallback on failure.
+- Valid single standard question, bounded names/compression/record lengths.
+  Responses require exact transaction ID, canonical question name/type/class,
+  QR/opcode, structural bounds, and (UDP) exact source IP/port. IDs are never
+  rewritten to disguise a mismatched reply.
+- Valid query + transport/auth/validation failure => local SERVFAIL; invalid query
+  => no response. Not a forged empty NOERROR success. A valid upstream TC answer
+  is preserved; a client's TCP retry follows the same configured proxy policy.
+- Per-flow source and original intercepted DNS destination are retained by
+  ipstack; returned DNS payload contains the original query ID and question.
+- Cancellation drops the exchange/session and semaphore permit; generation
+  TaskScope owns spawned packet-device work.
+- These limits bound this DNS layer, not all upstream ipstack memory: ipstack
+  1.0.1 uses unbounded ingress/session channels. General TUN queue bounding is a
+  separate outstanding resource-hardening item; no total-memory bound is claimed.
+
+## Validation scope
+
+Authored tests include pure bounds/correlation, unsupported UDP, no-fallback auth
+errors, concurrency/timeout/cancel release, TCP framing, bootstrap endpoint-only
+purpose guard and IPv6 bootstrap. Independent loopback test uses the already
+pinned official sing-vmess reference library with authenticated VMess AES-128-GCM,
+not a replacement production engine. It checks both DNS transports, A/AAAA,
+IPv4/IPv6 resolver targets, packet-device IPv4/IPv6 UDP ingress/reply association,
+wrong credentials/ID/question, cancellation, target counters and query SHA-256s.
+Host hooks allow only proxy sockets and the explicit bootstrap endpoint, not a
+direct user resolver socket.
+
+## Executed evidence (author candidate, not promoted/mobile acceptance)
+
+Evidence directory: `integration/proxy-dns-evidence` in the product workspace.
+Official test peer SHA-256:
+`eca989fc22cc8d1918e7fb3e0187e24a6207de31b138574ce8b5660053b55631`,
+matching the prior verified official-library build manifest. Go remains test-only.
+
+- vp-tun: **7 passed** (includes DNS source/size checks, pure constructor failure,
+  SERVFAIL/TCP framing, 64-exchange limit, timeout and cancellation resource release).
+- vp-core host_network: **4 passed**, including direct-user-DNS and unauthorized
+  bootstrap denial before the platform hook and zero destination traffic.
+- vp-dns full library: **25 passed; 4 public-live tests intentionally not run**.
+  Includes 9 wire tests and endpoint-bound IPv6 bootstrap response association.
+- TUIC peer-returned-domain denial: **1 passed**, zero bootstrap socket hooks/sends.
+- Independent authenticated VMess AES-128-GCM proxy/DNS/TUN test: **1 passed**;
+  explicit bootstrap target observed 21 queries, user IPv4 DNS target 13 and IPv6
+  target 6, exact query SHA-256s recorded, no disallowed platform-hook destination,
+  and zero remaining generation tasks. Includes real raw packet-device UDP v4/v6,
+  A/AAAA, both upstream transports, oversized DNS TC/TCP retry, wrong credential,
+  wrong ID/question, and cancellation after destination-observed forwarding.
+- Warnings-denied Clippy: **passed** vp-tun/vp-dns all targets and vp-core library.
+  Broader vp-core all-target check is **not clean**: pre-existing
+  `task_scope.rs:438` test triggers `clippy::async_yields_async`. Not suppressed
+  or changed in this patch. One pre-existing DNS test format string was modernized.
+- Formatting and diff whitespace checks: **passed** for changed sources.
+
+Initial concurrency unit test expected one Tokio yield to start all 64 tasks;
+61 had started. The test was repaired to await observed starts and await aborted
+join completion; production logic did not change. Initial/final logs are retained.
+Standalone std-only wire execution also passed all 9 tests before Cargo admission;
+that duplicate run is not counted as additional coverage.
+
+All Cargo runs used one job, incremental disabled, dev/test debuginfo zero, and
+shared `product-core-target`; no second full cache. Final runs were locked/offline.
+No host routes, firewalls, system proxy, trust stores, public DNS requests or real
+user domains were used. Actual syscall tracing is blocked and not bypassed;
+trusted hook and destination observations are **not** syscall evidence.
+
+**Not verified here:** merged/promotion identity, adapter schema2 build, native
+Android permission/lifecycle/DNS journey on a new artifact, Apple/Windows, full
+protocol/preset matrices, all-library IP-stack memory bounds or full-suite release.
+The adapter/host/settings owners must integrate the coordinated payload before
+this is the product default. Protected bootstrap lookup retains the existing
+A-record-only hostname lookup; numeric IPv6 proxy endpoints are supported.
+The raw UDP/TCP/DoT resolver verification helper also now enforces the same
+4096-byte/128-record bounds; larger messages are explicitly unsupported.
+Full privacy acceptance requires the coordinated native guest journey on the
+exact promoted artifact; the historical b739 APK is not upgraded by this evidence.
